#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186596622 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e43282c-0cf0-5b3e-8a8a-ad676b6134c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596100} {:answer/id #uuid "14511788-1583-59d2-b77f-e7cd0e3d763c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596111} {:answer/id #uuid "1a0978f6-2a63-5dec-9711-3250e7457b5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596119} {:answer/id #uuid "22b42229-2e2d-5606-bf7e-90c340abf4c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596133} {:answer/id #uuid "6c20b417-687c-5436-a128-a05c0b007a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c20b417-687c-5436-a128-a05c0b007a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596256} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd2731ad-3315-5e8a-9ee3-66123d65a523" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596606}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "08036111-0c20-583b-9b87-91af757f0cab" :question/math-academy-id "q-110757" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},$ and ${a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a basis of $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$  by inspection." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a basis of $S$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that spans $S.$\n\nFrom the given vectors, we can see that ${a}_{2}$ is a linear combination of vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=-3\\cdot {a}_{1}+0\\cdot {a}_{3}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the vector ${a}_{2}$ can be removed from $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ without changing the span. So $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is spanned by just $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{3}\\}.$ \n\nLastly, note that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent since they are not parallel. So the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set that spans $S.$\n\nTherefore, a basis of $S$ is $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{3}\\},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB=\\{{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}},{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186596645 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21ff4cbf-d10b-587a-9313-21d50adb5ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596132} {:answer/id #uuid "49ca982d-0247-572e-a0f5-a3887bcc99bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}26 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596199} {:answer/id #uuid "5352babd-73c2-5353-8571-1b5fb9d81589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}26 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596212} {:answer/id #uuid "5950f61e-cce8-51e9-acb6-abafe84a2dcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}26 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596221} {:answer/id #uuid "e8dd74f8-2931-5777-8cfb-fa0f5cb1787a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5352babd-73c2-5353-8571-1b5fb9d81589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}26 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596212} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1ea9610-1efe-5517-a4ae-7cc819f08b86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "38a7008b-1116-5fac-b1ec-aa79c81d6e02" :question/math-academy-id "q-110854" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},$ and ${a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}26 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}11 & 13 & 26 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, our matrix is already in a row echelon form.\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{3}\\},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}26 \\\\ 16 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186596655 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27256e8f-d3cf-59fb-8060-f42b95f9deab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596142} {:answer/id #uuid "29be70c2-9294-5715-9438-7c1153e924d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596146} {:answer/id #uuid "472a4b3c-e006-5386-844f-0ef2340eed4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596192} {:answer/id #uuid "6b832298-c453-5422-8bd4-7cf085e2ad4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596254} {:answer/id #uuid "b4135ea3-d99d-5a9d-8b47-a7b5f836b99f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29be70c2-9294-5715-9438-7c1153e924d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596146} :answer-field/id #uuid "080aaf41-1f60-5cca-9230-579fa1e8b02f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596495}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5b982763-01fc-513f-86c1-2bf91c0724be" :question/math-academy-id "q-110750" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},$ and ${a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a basis of $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ by inspection." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a basis of $S$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that spans $S.$\n\nFrom the given vectors, we can see that ${a}_{2}$ is a linear combination of vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=1\\cdot {a}_{1}+1\\cdot {a}_{3}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the vector ${a}_{2}$ can be removed from $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ without changing the span. So $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is spanned by just $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{3}\\}.$ \n\nLastly, note that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent since they are not parallel. So the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set that spans $S.$\n\nTherefore, a basis of $S$ is $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{3}\\},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB=\\{{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}},{{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186596666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a761d71-0562-59a6-ae91-872bf370da31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596224} {:answer/id #uuid "6b3c2351-6a2e-5dec-b72c-8412b6a16dee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596253} {:answer/id #uuid "7d307d12-7fdf-53ff-8d68-10bf29b50800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596280} {:answer/id #uuid "d00c3747-bb88-59fa-94b5-ca65232de916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596405} {:answer/id #uuid "d05522fd-eacc-55a5-9983-016429074252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b3c2351-6a2e-5dec-b72c-8412b6a16dee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596253} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e892215-29b1-513c-8eb3-bece5cb2c5be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "77074f06-1b98-5a52-b190-4d83a56a5953" :question/math-academy-id "q-110752" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},$ and ${a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a basis of $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ by inspection." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a basis of $S$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that spans $S.$\n\nFrom the given vectors, we can see that ${a}_{1}$ is a linear combination of vectors ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=1\\cdot {a}_{2}+1\\cdot {a}_{3}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the vector ${a}_{1}$ can be removed from $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ without changing the span. So $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is spanned by just $\\{{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$ \n\nLastly, note that ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent since they are not parallel. So the set $\\{{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set that spans $S.$\n\nTherefore, a basis of $S$ is $\\{{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB=\\{{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}},{{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186596671 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2de34826-3197-5763-9f6d-00da49a87109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596157} {:answer/id #uuid "30e945ce-c826-53be-98c0-a428b2bea1fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596160} {:answer/id #uuid "d853e65c-3bc5-5ba8-b280-fa912614ae6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}\\}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596427} {:answer/id #uuid "f3a1b199-58d2-5f05-a58f-821f7c55ae83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596468} {:answer/id #uuid "fb10e824-65ce-58f7-89ce-4435600e8f8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2de34826-3197-5763-9f6d-00da49a87109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596157} :answer-field/id #uuid "8691fad1-9b0c-5aa7-9100-7114002d965e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186596559}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7ab85b19-ea66-5456-84c6-6613c7c4d1ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-76336" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ ${a}_{3},$ and ${a}_{4}$ are given below. Determine whether $B=\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}\\}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3},$ where ${a}_{4}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{4}=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -52\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}\\}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+{x}_{3}{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -52\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3} &=-7 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=-21 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+8{x}_{3} &=-52\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 & -21 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 8 & -52\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 8 & -52\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-7){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the reduced matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}\\}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=-4,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=-3,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n(-4)\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+0\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+(-3)\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -52\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=(-4)+0+(-3)=-7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186602398 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8aa0b847-fd41-525b-b2b7-4775e68848b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -3.2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602181} {:answer/id #uuid "a9ec027c-573b-5f97-93b1-5dd3b386c79a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{2} & -3 & -3.2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602213} {:answer/id #uuid "ab487cca-0c1b-5007-8aa1-cefa0ab6da91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602215} {:answer/id #uuid "eda78da6-b105-5a45-b2b2-92e1365bd9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602283} {:answer/id #uuid "fd572836-2b5a-5753-ad3e-9e587ec0980c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eda78da6-b105-5a45-b2b2-92e1365bd9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602283} :answer-field/id #uuid "c592bb5c-24f7-5084-9ea9-7b8dd506a403" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0c77e397-1dac-5cc0-805f-37617d73f66e" :question/math-academy-id "q-41953" :question/problem "Find the product $AB$, if\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand \n$$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & -3 & -3.2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is the $1$st *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $B$ by the $1$st *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}$ on the *left*, the result must be the $1$st *row* of $B.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & -3 & -3.2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186602405 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3deb735b-59de-514c-a9c5-d0a2f271c925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186602111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uu